# A VS match settled after "Go!": Yoshi (P1) vs Yoshi (P2) on Onett, no input,
# so both stand at their spawn points. Authored to give Yoshi -- and his Egg
# Lay egg -- a reference; the shipped match case is Pikachu vs Peach and never
# puts a Yoshi on screen.
#
# Same route as match.case (Dolphin cannot be booted into a match; the
# boot-to-mode patches leave it on the Main Menu), with only the character
# picks changed. The CSS grid is
#     row 1: Mario Pikachu Bowser Peach Yoshi DK C.Falcon
#     row 2: Fox Ness IceClimbers Kirby Samus Zelda Link
# Icon pitch measured off a Dolphin dump is ~65 px at 640 wide and the hand
# moves ~7.5 px/frame at full deflection, so a column is ~8.7 frames -- which
# is why match.case's single 10-frame nudge moves exactly one icon.
#
# P1's hand starts over column 1 and P2's over column 3 (that is how the same
# movement lands match.case on Pikachu and Peach). Yoshi is column 5, so P1
# travels 4 columns and P2 travels 2.
#
# The hand accelerates rather than moving at a constant rate, so the frames
# are not proportional to the distance: a first pass with P1 held right for
# 35 frames overshot to Donkey Kong (5 columns, 9.3 px/frame averaged) while
# P2's 18 frames covered 2 columns (7.2 px/frame). P1 is held 30.
#
# Everything after the picks is match.case's stage-select route shifted +40
# frames to make room, so ref_lead moves with it.
#
# Costumes: picking the same character for both players makes the CSS hand
# the second one a different costume, so the reference is green Yoshi (P1)
# against red Yoshi (P2) and the port has to be told colour 1 for P2. A
# different costume is a different texture set, which swamps a frame diff.
description: VS match settled, Yoshi vs Yoshi on Onett
run_frames: 360
ref_frames: 2400
align: search
window: 8
ref_lead: -1570
env: MELEE_BOOT_MODE=14
env: MELEE_BOOT_MATCH=17,17,9,0,1
ref_input: 236:+START
ref_input: 240:-START
ref_input: 400:+START
ref_input: 404:-START
ref_input: 760:MAIN:0.5:0.0
ref_input: 768:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 820:+A
ref_input: 824:-A
ref_input: 950:+A
ref_input: 954:-A
ref_input: 1000:P2:+A
ref_input: 1004:P2:-A
ref_input: 1060:MAIN:0.5:1.0
ref_input: 1120:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1130:MAIN:1.0:0.5
ref_input: 1160:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1175:MAIN:0.5:0.0
ref_input: 1182:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1195:+A
ref_input: 1199:-A
ref_input: 1210:P2:MAIN:0.5:1.0
ref_input: 1270:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1280:P2:MAIN:1.0:0.5
ref_input: 1298:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1308:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.0
ref_input: 1315:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1328:P2:+A
ref_input: 1332:P2:-A
ref_input: 1380:+START
ref_input: 1384:-START
ref_input: 1460:MAIN:0.5:1.0
ref_input: 1492:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1520:+A
ref_input: 1524:-A
checks: 250, 320
